I think the key to archaeologists is that they have speed from the 
beginning.  Meaning you should run away from everything that is too 
tough for you.  (Of course the advice of switching to the pick-axe as 
your main weapon immediately is good, but that alone will not be 
sufficient for survival, because a pick-axe is not a particularly good 
weapon.)

Another boon is that they can identify gems fairly easily and will 
therefore be able to buy protection or equipment (instead of waiting for 
their pets to steal it).  I used to keep one hard gem to be able to 
engrave Elbereth, but it is a slow process this way, usually not useful 
to save you from a desperate situation.

I started trying for an ascension with archaeologists first and wasted 
six of them.  The seventh escaped the dungeon with a 6 million score - 
he had lost the Book of the Dead irretrievably in the moat around the 
wizard's tower after freezing and digging out the place (this was NH 
3.1.3).  The eighth ascended (I had ascended a valk in between), the 
ninth, too, and I think I haven't played additional ones. I consider 
them a fairly easy class in the meantime (but that may have changed, 
there may be new difficulties with newer versions of the game).

